---
description: Testing and completion rules for extension and shared-package changes.
globs: ["apps/**/*", "packages/**/*", "scripts/**/*"]
alwaysApply: false
---

A code change is not complete because it builds once.

- Add or update tests in the same change when behavior changes.
- Unit-test pure logic, parsing, state transitions, storage adapters, permission decisions, message validation, and theme utilities.
- E2E-test extension runtime behavior: load/install, popup/options/sidepanel, content-script injection, background messaging, storage persistence, permissions, theme switching, and critical host integrations.
- Include negative/failure cases for third-party DOM changes and destructive operations.
- Run `pnpm verify:repo`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, and relevant `pnpm test:e2e` checks before declaring completion.
- Never suppress a failing check merely to make CI green. Fix the cause or document a deliberate exception in the app QA document.
